<%# `lexxy-content`, not the `trix-content` that `action_text:install` generates.

    Lexxy's content stylesheet is written entirely as `:where(.lexxy-content)`,
    so with the stock wrapper class none of it applies to a PUBLISHED post —
    including the code-token colours. The editor would highlight a code block
    and the published page would show the same block flat, which defeats the
    point of a WYSIWYG editor.

    Everything in that stylesheet has zero specificity by construction, so the
    `.prose` rules in application.css still win wherever DW-001 disagrees. %>
<div class="lexxy-content">
  <%= yield -%>
</div>
